TITLE='Authentic title "Average 401K Balance By Age - 2026 Edition!" is a search-style benchmark query with a year tag. The script turns the query against itself: it argues the average is a "Phantom Saver", gives medians by age, then shifts to coverage gaps, leakage, defaults and two-tier Roth outcomes. TYPICAL against the cohort. Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a white polo, smirking and pointing right. Right: a heavy black headline "ARE YOU BEHIND?" above five ascending green coin stacks labelled 20s, 30s, 40s, 50s and 60s, with a red dotted growth arrow. At 320x180 the headline, stacks and decade labels stay legible. The thumbnail asks the exact question the script rejects at the end ("stop asking am I behind").'
SCRIPT='A data-driven essay with composites Jem, Trevor and Gary: late-night search hook; Vanguard HAS average vs median; Phantom Saver; medians by age; balances converted to annuity income; survivorship (BLS access, Fed/SCF non-savers); job tenure and forgotten accounts; retirement income gap; $1.26M magic number; trust-fund depletion; lived experience; community plug; leakage (hardship withdrawals, cash-outs, fees, 3% defaults); Thiel Roth and mega-Roths; record balances as market weather; lower return forecasts; three actions (match, default rate, 2026 limits); millionaire survivorship; Jem raises her rate from 3% to 6%. Directly verified: IRS 2026 limits including the 60-63 replace-not-stack rule; BLS 72% access (post-publication release, consistent). Search-only: Vanguard $167,970/$44,115. Wrong framing: the trust-fund date is called "not a prediction" (it is a projection; the 2025 report said 2033). Most arithmetic reproduces. The stored ending is complete.'
BEATS=['Hook: Jem and Trevor read the same number.','Vanguard average vs median; Phantom Saver.','Open loop: the default number.','Medians by age; phantom comparison.','Under $10K and over $250K shares; annuity conversion.','Survivorship: access, participation, non-savers.','Job tenure and forgotten 401(k)s.','Gary open loop; mega-Roth open loop.','Income gap in retirement.','Magic number vs median.','Trust-fund depletion.','Lived experience; risk shift; community plug.','Hardship withdrawals; cash-outs; fees.','Auto-enrollment defaults.','Thiel Roth; mega-Roths.','Records as market weather; forecasts.','Actions: match, default rate, limits.','Trevor and Gary revisited.','Jem changes 3% to 6%; close and plug.']
